    <h2>FAQ</h2>

    <h3>Is Squarespace better than Wix?</h3>
    <p>Squarespace is better if you want polished templates, a clean editor, and predictable design output. Wix is better if you want drag-and-drop flexibility, more apps, and a lower entry price. For portfolios, restaurants, and brand-led sites, Squarespace wins. For small businesses that need custom layouts and third-party apps, Wix wins.</p>

    <h3>Which is cheaper, Squarespace or Wix?</h3>
    <p>Wix is cheaper at the entry level. Wix Light starts at $17 per month with no ads and a custom domain, while Squarespace Personal starts at $16 per month. However, Wix often runs first-year discounts that bring the effective price below $10. For e-commerce, Squarespace Business at $23 per month is cheaper than Wix Business at $32 per month.</p>

    <h3>Can I switch templates on Squarespace after launch?</h3>
    <p>Yes, but content may reflow unpredictably. Squarespace 7.1 uses a unified template system, so switching templates keeps your content but changes layout and typography. You may need to adjust spacing and images after switching. Wix does not use templates in the same way once you start editing, so changing design means rebuilding the site.</p>

    <h3>Does Wix have better SEO than Squarespace?</h3>
    <p>Both have strong SEO features including customizable meta tags, sitemaps, and SSL. Wix offers more granular control with SEO patterns, structured data, and a built-in SEO checklist. Squarespace has cleaner URLs by default and better mobile performance. For most users, SEO performance depends more on content than on the platform.</p>

    <h3>Which is better for e-commerce?</h3>
    <p>Squarespace is better for small to mid-sized stores with strong visual branding. Its commerce plans include unlimited products, zero transaction fees, and integrated inventory. Wix is better for larger stores that need app-based extensions, multi-channel selling, and custom checkout. For stores under 100 products, Squarespace wins. For stores over 100 products, Wix wins.</p>

    <h3>Can I use Squarespace and Wix together?</h3>
    <p>You can host different sites on different platforms, but you cannot merge a Squarespace site with a Wix site. A common setup is Squarespace for the main brand site and Wix for a specific landing page or microsite that needs custom layout. Most users pick one platform to avoid managing two subscriptions and design systems.</p>

